{
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "published": "2026-11-04",
  "changelog": [
    "**Every inflatable is now a real game model.** All seventy (the sixty-one figures and nine walkway arches) ship in `stream/` as fused one-skin drawables with an emissive shader, a point light and sphere collision, generated from the same shapes that used to be drawn per frame (`tools/build-inflatables.py` \u2192 Blender/Sollumz \u2192 `tools/cwconv`). They cast shadows, take the game's lighting, and you bump into them. The Inflatables tab now places the model and shows its picture; each comes in the one size on its card. The catalog lists them from the generated `shared/inflatable_models.lua`, so only models actually present in `stream/` are offered. Download size grows by about 37 MB.",
    "Inflatables placed with earlier versions are still drawn the old way and still inflate, deflate and sway; the Edit tray still toggles them.",
    "Walkway arch models align their rows along the path, like the drawn arches did.",
    "**Inflatable models are solid** (Settings -> Inflatables and wreaths): on, players and vehicles bump into them; off, everything passes through, for a server whose doorways and walks keep getting blocked. Applies to every client at once.",
    "**Clear every decoration on the server** (Locations tab, admins): one armed control takes down every location and holiday at once, same as `/holiday clear all`. Saved layouts are kept, and the server writes `data/decorations.json.before-clear-<time>` first so a wrong click can be undone.",
    "Pictures for the seventy models ship rendered from their shapes; `/holiday thumbs` replaces them with in-game photographs as before.",
    "`publish-release.ps1` (vendor): hand it the escrowed zip from Keymaster and it checks the escrow, writes `update.json`, commits, tags, pushes and attaches the zip to a GitHub Release."
  ],
